\begin{proof}
Take arbitrary residue classes $\bar a,\bar b,\bar c\in\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z$, with representatives $a,b,c\in\mathbb Z$. By the definition of addition of residue classes and associativity in $\mathbb Z$,
\[
\begin{aligned}
(\bar a+\bar b)+\bar c
&=\overline{a+b}+\bar c
=\overline{(a+b)+c}
=\overline{a+(b+c)}\\
&=\bar a+\overline{b+c}
=\bar a+(\bar b+\bar c).
\end{aligned}
\]
Therefore addition on $\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z$ is associative.
\end{proof}

